T('multiday','Multiple-session continuation',85,'28',[10,10.2,10.5,10.4,10.6,10.9,11.3,11.6,12.1,12.8],'The guide includes multiday continuation and parabolic examples. This scenario explicitly divides fictional bars into separate sessions; OHLC is not historical.',['Assume bars 1–5 are session one and 6–10 session two. What is observed?','Higher fictional prices in the second session','Proof that every overnight hold works','No price movement between sessions','The supplied later closes exceed the early range.','One illustration cannot establish overnight profitability.','The supplied values differ.'],['Why state session boundaries?','To avoid confusing an intraday pattern with cross-session context','To guarantee the next session opens higher','To make all liquidity concerns vanish','Session definitions affect interpretation.','A boundary cannot guarantee the next open.','Session labels do not establish liquidity.']),
T('short-squeeze','Short-squeeze context',87,'30',[10,10.2,10.5,11,12,13.5,15.5,18,20.5,22],'The source labels a short-squeeze example. Our chart illustrates rapid upside; actual short positioning cannot be inferred from candles alone.',['What cannot be verified from this steep rise alone?','The actual short positions and forced covering behind it','The displayed upward progression','That the latest fictional close is above the first','Positioning requires information beyond this chart.','The upward progression is displayed.','The supplied closes support that comparison.'],['Why does shorting an extended rise still need a risk plan?','Extension does not impose a fixed upper price limit','A steep chart guarantees immediate collapse','Every short loss is capped at its premium','An underlying stock can continue rising.','No immediate reversal is assured.','Short stock is not a fully paid long option.']),
T('no-news-halt','Unverified catalyst and halt context',88,'31a',[10,10.4,10.9,11.5,12.3,13.4,12.8,11.9,11,10.7],'The guide labels no-news squeezes and halts on pages 88–89. This is source labeling, not a new verification of the historical events or current exchange rules.',['If this illustration supplies no verified catalyst, what does the spike establish?','A price rise, not independently verified news','A confirmed company announcement','Proof that the exchange will never pause trading','The price move is visible but news is not verified here.','A candle chart is not an announcement source.','A spike cannot exclude a pause.'],['What is a defensible practice response under a verified-catalyst requirement?','Wait or skip until that requirement can be checked','Infer a catalyst from green candles','Assume a pause guarantees a favorable resumption','The stated information condition is unmet.','Green candles are not independent evidence of news.','Resumption direction and fills remain uncertain.'])

